# Tier 57 -- PoC 3 phase 5, the bundle. JSON only: what
# scripts/verify_racelab_bundle.py found on a FRESH CLONE of the
# poc3-racelab-demo branch, one record per platform -- the mode run.sh has in
# the index, its line endings as checked out, the blob-hash identity of every
# copied file against the commit SOURCE_COMMITS names, the scans, and (with
# --launch) the launcher's own self-test. tests/test_tier57_racelab_bundle.py
# reads them. Rebuilding a record costs a build (about a minute), a clone, and
# with --launch a full install into a fresh .venv: minutes with a warm pip
# cache, and a few hundred megabytes of downloads without one. The launch logs
# beside them are ignored.
!out/racelab_bundle/
out/racelab_bundle/*
!out/racelab_bundle/verify_*.json

# The car editor's leavings. The geometry ITSELF is tracked -- it is the car --
# but its rolling backup, the tracing backdrops and the check's picture are not.
atlas/cases/car_geometry.json.bak
out/backdrops/
out/car_geometry.png
out/editor.log

# Tier 65 -- the body-fitted column declared and compiled
# (`tier65_car_graph.py --out out/racelab14`). JSON only: the record layer's
# refusal of a port-less expert, the composite's interpolation rows, the compile
# of the joined / disjoint / clocks-reconciled / one-join-at-a-time variants
# beside the porous column's, the strip bond against Tier 64's march, and the
# verdicts. Rebuilding costs about two and a half minutes, nearly all of it the
# composite the record stage builds to count its rows. The run logs beside it
# are ignored.
!out/racelab14/
out/racelab14/*
!out/racelab14/racelab14.json

# Tier 66 -- the body-fitted composite on one raster, the demo's field overlay
# (`tier66_car_render.py --out out/racelab15`). The JSON carries the operator's
# cost and mask at three rasters, the two controls, what the background alone
# could not draw, and the checks on the operator; `overlay_speed.png` is the
# frame the page shows, kept because it is the deliverable and it is 40 KB.
# Rebuilding costs about seven minutes, most of it building the operator at
# three resolutions on a composite that takes a minute to assemble.
!out/racelab15/
out/racelab15/*
!out/racelab15/racelab15.json
!out/racelab15/overlay_speed.png

# Tier 67 -- where a learned expert can sit on the body-fitted column
# (`tier67_car_windows.py --out out/racelab16`). JSON only: every 128 x 128
# placement on the background under both admissibility tests, the greedy tilings
# under four declared orders, the ceiling expressed against the composite's
# unknowns, and one window taken out and put back. Rebuilding costs about two
# minutes, nearly all of it the composite the first stage builds.
!out/racelab16/
out/racelab16/*
!out/racelab16/racelab16.json

# Tier 68 -- the body-fitted car as a demo column, and the caches that start it
# (`tier68_bodyfitted_demo.py --out out/racelab17`). JSON only: the build with
# both caches warm, the evidence that a device-free release sits outside the
# machine's envelope and a settled one does not, every field drawn and every
# field refused with its reason, and the validator run against the car's own
# operator.
#
# `out/cache/` is NOT committed and is not meant to be: the probe operator is
# 6.7 MB and the settled state 15 MB, both are derived, and both rebuild --
# the operator in 63 s and the settled state in a settle march. They are
# caches, not records.
!out/racelab17/
out/racelab17/*
!out/racelab17/racelab17.json

# Tier 69 -- section 3.3's parameters and what each one actually reaches
# (`tier69_car_knobs.py --out out/racelab18`). JSON only: every knob moved end
# to end with the quantity it claims to reach measured at both, the
# motor-generator's repair, and the 40-artifact byte control with what this
# tier added to the moved set (nothing).
!out/racelab18/
out/racelab18/*
!out/racelab18/racelab18.json

# Tier 70 -- rake and the duct area wired, and the knob layer criterion 2
# needs (tier70_knobs_wired.py --out out/racelab19). JSON only: the reach
# tally with both knobs in, every offerable knob moved with the subsystems
# that responded, the four refusals, and the fingerprint check that says
# wiring them did not move the nominal car.
!out/racelab19/
out/racelab19/*
!out/racelab19/racelab19.json

# Tier 71 -- the dashboard, and the coolant knob that finally reaches the
# march (tier71_dashboard.py --out out/racelab20). JSON only: LoopSettings
# threaded through the legs and CarUnion, the constants left untouched by a
# full reach report, the weight hash moving with the knob, the 40-artifact
# byte control, and a geometry commit end to end.
!out/racelab20/
out/racelab20/*
!out/racelab20/racelab20.json

# Tier 72 -- the fixed point the implicit step has, and the certified mode on
# it (tier72_certified_step.py --out out/racelab21). JSON only: existence and
# reachability of the momentum solve's fixed point for all three sweeps on the
# cylinder and the car, every cheap map against one classical answer, the
# certified step against the classical step, and why Poseidon-T could not be
# called at this column's time step.
!out/racelab21/
out/racelab21/*
!out/racelab21/racelab21.json

# Tier 73 -- the certified mode on the screen, section 12's criterion 4
# (tier73_certified_screen.py --out out/racelab22). JSON only: every certified
# step's outer/inner/residual over a live march, the measured error against the
# classical answer with verify on, the mode's price and the verification's
# price kept apart, a certified march against a classical one from the same
# settled state with its positive control, and a knob moved while certified.
!out/racelab22/
out/racelab22/*
!out/racelab22/racelab22.json

# Tier 74 -- showable: the bundle carrying the column it claims to
# (tier74_showable.py --out out/racelab23). JSON only: the commit refusal with
# its control and the car it names, the bundle's lists checked closed, what the
# body-fitted demo reads from disk, the fresh build's scans, and the two
# columns on their own ports.
!out/racelab23/
out/racelab23/*
!out/racelab23/racelab23.json

# Tier 80 -- CS-21's multirate lag defect
# (w314_rocket_multirate_defect.py --json out/w314.json). 15 KB, JSON only:
# the R9 decisions, the slope stage's constants with the interval-independence
# check CS-11 never ran, the sigma law at a pinned 50:1 with its bitwise-zero
# single-rate control, CS-11's own ratio control at full precision (so the
# "exactly 1.000000" reading can be checked against a floor), the rank-1-trace
# and two-way arms, the transfer control against CS-11's published constants,
# and the anchor at the declared exchange interval.
#
# It is force-included because `tests/test_tier80_multirate_defect.py` READS it
# -- four gate tests skip without it -- and section 14 cites it line by line.
# **Nothing from Tiers 76-79 is tracked**, though the rule at the top of this
# block says the current case study's artifacts are, and CS-21 is it: so on a
# clone, none of sections 6-13's numbers can be checked against the run that
# produced them. Recorded rather than fixed here, because re-running four
# tiers' artifacts is not this tier's scope.
!out/w314.json

# Tier 81 -- W305 (w305_trajectory_and_mech.py --json out/w305.json). ~6 KB,
# JSON only: the b-c MECH spectrum with its tolerance sweep, the rigid-load
# map, the trajectory agent's probed block against its closed form, the
# composed c-trajectory seam, and the one-sidedness checks read off the solver.
!out/w305.json

