# The Atlas Workbench's run records.  The runner writes one JSON per run beside
# each case file (out/workbench/cases/<case>.results/), and those stay local;
# the ones a wiki page quotes are copied into out/workbench/records/, which is
# committed.  Each is the case as it marched, every per-step time, each check
# with its registered tolerance, and the machine's state (power, other Python
# processes).  Small: 10-20 KB a run.
!out/workbench/
out/workbench/*
!out/workbench/records/
# The one-command install's verification logs stay local: each record in
# out/workbench/records/installer/ keeps the tail of every log it ran.
out/workbench/records/installer/logs/
# The learned case (demo item 1.5): its registration, step 0, the truth run (on
# the D/16 grid it is compared on), the training log, the gate's records and the
# weights are committed. The training data is not: tens of GB, generated on the
# rented box from the registered seeds, and reproducible from them.
!out/learned-case/
out/learned-case/data/
# The proposal website (W354): the S-channel's export for the site's "How it works"
# section, written by scripts/site_export_schannel.py and cited by site/data/claims.json.
!out/site/

# The workbench launchers at the root (run.sh, run.cmd) build this; deleting it
# undoes the whole install.
.venv/
